.page passwd 1 change a password

# SYNOPSIS
*passwd* [_USER_]

# DESCRIPTION
`passwd` changes the password of the caller (or, for root, of _USER_). Unless the account has no password yet it first asks for the current one. The new password is asked for twice without echo; leaving it empty removes the password, which means the account can be entered without one. The password is stored in shadow(5) as a salted SHA-256 hash, never as typed. `passwd` is installed setuid root.

Nothing is stored permanently yet: `/Hakurei/etc` lives in memory and is rebuilt from the boot image at every start, so a changed password lasts until the next restart.

# EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if the check failed, the two entries differ, or the file cannot be written.

# SEE ALSO
su(1), login(1), shadow(5), accounts(7)
